1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,280
Let's set up your development environment.

2
00:00:02,280 --> 00:00:04,920
You'll need Python 3.10 or higher.

3
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:06,760
Create a virtual environment,

4
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:09,120
then install the dependencies solders

5
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:12,680
for Solana transaction signing, requests for API calls,

6
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:16,720
Python.10 for configuration, base 58 for key encoding,

7
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:18,720
and web sockets for the real-time connection

8
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:19,960
to pump portal.

9
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:22,560
All of this installs with a single pip command.

10
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:25,480
Your configuration lives in a .env file,

11
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:26,760
which we'll set up next.

1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,680
The .envave file is your bot's control panel.

2
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:10,440
Starting amount is $2 USDC, a safe amount to learn with.

3
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:17,960
Stop loss is set to 0.82, meaning you'll exit if the token drops 18% from your entry.

4
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:25,200
Slippage is 150 basis points or 1.5%, the bot polls price every 8 seconds.

5
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:31,200
After 2 consecutive losses, it pauses for 5 minutes to avoid bleeding in bad market conditions.

6
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:36,680
And the play floor of $1 prevents the death spiral, where one early loss permanently cripples

7
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:37,680
your bankroll.

8
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:40,040
Always start with dry run set to true.

1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,600
RPC setup. You need a dedicated Solana wallet for the bot. Never use your main wallet.

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:11,760
Create one with Phantom or the Solana CLI. Export the private key as a base 58 string

3
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:18,720
and paste it in your .nv file. For your RPC endpoint get a free tier from Alchemy Orhelius.

4
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:23,840
Don't use the default mainnet beta endpoint. It's rate limited and slow. Fund the wallet

5
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:28,080
with a small amount of USDC for trades and sold for gas fees.

1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,240
Slide 8 Token Scanner WebSocket. This is where the magic happens.

2
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:09,360
The Token Scanner connects to the Pump Portal WebSocket and subscribes to new token events.

3
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:15,040
The moment someone creates a new token on Pump.fun, we get notified with the mint address, name,

4
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:20,320
symbol and how much SOL the developer bought at launch. This happens in under one second.

5
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:25,360
Compare that to polling deck screener every 30 seconds where you'd miss the first wave of

6
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:28,880
buyers entirely. Speed is everything in this game.

1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,050
Let's talk about the timing.

2
00:00:02,050 --> 00:00:06,050
Token detection happens in under 1 second via WebSocket.

3
00:00:06,050 --> 00:00:11,050
Then we wait 25 seconds for DeX screener to index the pair and give us liquidity and volume data.

4
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:14,050
The entire scan window is up to 15 minutes.

5
00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:19,050
If no qualifying token is found in that time, the bot starts a new scan cycle.

6
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:24,050
If the WebSocket disconnects, it automatically reconnects with exponential backoff,

7
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:26,050
cycling through multiple endpoints.

8
00:00:26,050 --> 00:00:29,050
It never silently falls asleep.

1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,720
Rug detection. Before buying anything, the bot runs four safety checks.

2
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:09,200
First, scam name detection. If the token name contains words like guaranteed,

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:13,760
100x, airdrop or safe moon, it skipped immediately.

4
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:18,960
Second, honeypot detection. If there are 50 plus buys but fewer than two cells,

5
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:23,440
that means nobody can sell, it's a trap. Third, wash trading.

6
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:28,320
If the 5 minute volume is 50 times the liquidity, that activity is fake.

7
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:33,120
Fourth, dev dump check. If the developer bought more than 20 sol at launch,

8
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:36,240
they loaded their bag and will likely dump on everyone else.

9
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:39,840
Any one of these flags means we skipped the token.

1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,520
Filter thresholds. Even after passing rug checks, tokens must meet strict criteria.

2
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:10,400
Maximum age, 5 minutes. If it's been around longer, the easy gains are gone.

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:17,440
Liquidity must be between $2,500,000, enough to trade, but not so much that we're late.

4
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:23,200
Minimum 5 minute volume is $500. We need at least 12 transactions in 5 minutes,

5
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:29,120
with at least 8 of those being buys. The buy to sell ratio must be at least 1.3x,

6
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:34,720
meaning buyers are dominating and market cap can't exceed 10 million. We want to be early.

1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,840
Slide 12, token scoring.

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:04,200
Not all qualifying tokens are equal,

3
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:06,480
so we score them from zero to 100.

4
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:08,680
Freshness gives up to 10 points.

5
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:11,360
Tokens under two minutes old get the maximum.

6
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:13,680
Bipressure is worth up to 25 points

7
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:15,480
based on the buy-sell ratio.

8
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:17,400
Volume contributes up to 20 points

9
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:18,800
on a logarithmic scale.

10
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:22,280
Liquidity in the sweet spot of $5,000 to $50,000

11
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:23,840
earns 15 points.

12
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:26,760
An affair launch where the developer bought little

13
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:30,000
or no sell initially adds up to 10 points.

14
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,040
The higher the score,

15
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:33,240
the stronger our conviction in the trade.

1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,600
Slide 13 – Jupiter Swaps

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,120
Jupiter is Solana Swap Aggregator.

3
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:12,520
It finds the best route across all DEXs, Radium, Orca, Meteora and more for a single transaction.

4
00:00:12,520 --> 00:00:14,320
Our buy flow has four steps.

5
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:18,320
One, get a quote, how many tokens we'll receive for our USDC.

6
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:20,080
Two, build the swap transaction.

7
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:23,560
Three, sign it with our private key and broadcast to the network.

8
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:26,480
Four, confirm the transaction landed on chain.

9
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:29,000
For sales, it's the same process in reverse.

10
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:36,400
If a cell fails due to low liquidity, we escalate slippage from 200 to 500 to 1,000 basis points

11
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:38,000
before giving up.

1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,040
Price monitoring and exits.

2
00:00:02,040 --> 00:00:05,880
Once we're in a position, the bot pulls the price every 8 seconds.

3
00:00:05,880 --> 00:00:11,520
Our take profit target is 2x, meaning we sell when the token doubles from our entry price.

4
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:15,600
Stop loss is at 0.82x and 18% loss.

5
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:20,240
Dex screener is the primary price source because it also gives us liquidity data.

6
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:23,280
If Dex screener fails, we fall back to Jupiter quotes.

7
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:28,120
If liquidity drops below $25, the pool is effectively dead and we trigger dead

8
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:31,040
pool handling instead of retrying forever.

1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,600
Light 15, compounding strategy, here's where it gets exciting.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,880
Every time the bot wins, it splits the proceeds.

3
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:09,760
60% goes back into the next trade.

4
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:12,000
40% is saved permanently.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,560
Start with $2.

6
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:15,320
The token doubles to four.

7
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:18,800
Save $1.60, reinvest $2.40.

8
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:21,680
Next win, $2.40 becomes $4.80.

9
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:24,880
Save $1.92, reinvest $2.88.

10
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:27,280
On a win streak, this compounds rapidly.

11
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:29,200
The bot runs up to 30 cycles

12
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:30,880
even with a modest win rate.

13
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:33,600
The compounding math works in your favor over time.

