1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,600
16. Risk management. Three safety features keep the bot alive.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,400
Number one, the play floor.

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:09,400
If your trade amount drops below $1 after a loss,

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:11,360
it resets to your starting amount.

5
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:13,440
This is the single most important feature.

6
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:14,840
Without it, one early loss

7
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:17,120
permanently cripples every future cycle.

8
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:19,400
Number two, the last pause.

9
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:23,400
After two consecutive losses, the bot waits five minutes.

10
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:25,760
Bad market conditions tend to cluster,

11
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:27,880
so this prevents bleeding.

12
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:30,520
Number three, dead pool detection.

13
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:33,960
If a token's liquidity drops below $25,

14
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:35,760
the bot stops trying to sell

15
00:00:35,760 --> 00:00:38,160
and backs off to 10 minute rechecks.

16
00:00:38,160 --> 00:00:40,160
No point hammering a dead pool.

1
